<chapter id="doltgres-config">
 <title>Versioned Storage Configuration</title>

 <para>
  This chapter describes the configuration parameters of the versioned
  storage, beside those of <xref linkend="runtime-config"/>.
 </para>

 <sect1 id="doltgres-config-resource">
  <title>Resource Consumption</title>

  <variablelist>
   <varlistentry id="guc-delta-memory" xreflabel="delta_memory">
    <term><varname>delta_memory</varname> (<type>integer</type>)
    <indexterm>
     <primary><varname>delta_memory</varname> configuration parameter</primary>
    </indexterm>
    </term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Sets the amount of shared memory the versioned storage uses for recent
      changes, which the server allocates at start beside
      <xref linkend="guc-shared-buffers"/>, as the region
      <literal>versioned delta</literal> of
      <link linkend="view-pg-shmem-allocations"><structname>pg_shmem_allocations</structname></link>.
      If this value is specified without units, it is taken as kilobytes.
      It is used in whole blocks of 64 kilobytes, rounded down.
      The default is 32 megabytes (<literal>32MB</literal>), and the minimum
      is 1 megabyte (<literal>1MB</literal>).
      Beside it the server takes fixed shared memory sized from this setting
      and not counted in it, under 1% of it.
      This parameter can only be set at server start.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>

   <varlistentry id="guc-node-cache-size" xreflabel="node_cache_size">
    <term><varname>node_cache_size</varname> (<type>integer</type>)
    <indexterm>
     <primary><varname>node_cache_size</varname> configuration parameter</primary>
    </indexterm>
    </term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Sets the amount of shared memory the versioned storage uses to cache
      its tables' and indexes' tree nodes, which the server allocates at start
      beside <xref linkend="guc-shared-buffers"/>, as the region
      <literal>versioned node cache</literal> of
      <link linkend="view-pg-shmem-allocations"><structname>pg_shmem_allocations</structname></link>.
      If this value is specified without units, it is taken as kilobytes.
      The default is 128 megabytes (<literal>128MB</literal>), and the minimum
      is 1 megabyte (<literal>1MB</literal>).
      This parameter can only be set at server start.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>
  </variablelist>
 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="doltgres-config-developer">
  <title>Developer Options</title>

  <para>
   The following parameters are intended for developer testing, and should
   never be used on a production database.  As such, they have been excluded
   from the sample <filename>postgresql.conf</filename> file.
  </para>

  <variablelist>
   <varlistentry id="guc-debug-fail-preload-allocation" xreflabel="debug_fail_preload_allocation">
    <term><varname>debug_fail_preload_allocation</varname> (<type>enum</type>)
    <indexterm>
     <primary><varname>debug_fail_preload_allocation</varname> configuration parameter</primary>
    </indexterm>
    </term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Makes the versioned storage's first allocation fail when a process
      starts, so that tests can check that the failure is reported as an
      <literal>out of memory</literal> error rather than crashing the server.
      The allowed values are <literal>off</literal> (the default), which
      fails nothing; <literal>postmaster</literal>, which fails it in the
      postmaster, so the server fails to start with an
      <literal>out of memory</literal> <literal>FATAL</literal> error; and
      <literal>child</literal>, which fails it in each process the postmaster
      starts.  The <literal>child</literal> value takes effect only in
      servers built with <symbol>EXEC_BACKEND</symbol> (see
      <xref linkend="guc-debug-exec-backend"/>), since only there does each
      child process run the preload step itself; elsewhere it fails nothing.
      This parameter can only be set at server start.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>
  </variablelist>
 </sect1>
 <sect1 id="doltgres-config-collector">
  <title>Collection</title>

  <para>
   The collector, a background worker, removes the chunks of the versioned
   storage that no reader can reach. These parameters set when it runs and
   how fast. Each can be set only in the <filename>postgresql.conf</filename>
   file or on the server command line.
  </para>

  <variablelist>
   <varlistentry id="guc-collector-first-packs" xreflabel="collector_first_packs">
    <term><varname>collector_first_packs</varname> (<type>integer</type>)
    <indexterm>
     <primary><varname>collector_first_packs</varname> configuration parameter</primary>
    </indexterm>
    </term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Sets how many packs a database's versioned storage holds before the
      collector's first full collection of it runs on its own. Doltgrust's
      <literal>FIRST_COLLECTION_PACKS</literal>. The default is 64.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>

   <varlistentry id="guc-collector-full-interval" xreflabel="collector_full_interval">
    <term><varname>collector_full_interval</varname> (<type>integer</type>)
    <indexterm>
     <primary><varname>collector_full_interval</varname> configuration parameter</primary>
    </indexterm>
    </term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Sets the longest time between full collections of a database's versioned
      storage. If this value is specified without units, it is taken as
      seconds. Doltgrust's <literal>FULL_EVERY</literal>. The default is one
      day (<literal>1d</literal>).
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>

   <varlistentry id="guc-collector-io-limit" xreflabel="collector_io_limit">
    <term><varname>collector_io_limit</varname> (<type>integer</type>)
    <indexterm>
     <primary><varname>collector_io_limit</varname> configuration parameter</primary>
    </indexterm>
    </term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Sets the most bytes a second a collection reads and copies while the
      database's packs are within
      <xref linkend="guc-collector-target-percent"/> of their live bytes; past
      it collections run unpaced. If this
      value is specified without units, it is taken as kilobytes a second.
      Zero, the default, sets no limit. Doltgrust's
      <literal>io_limit</literal>.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>

   <varlistentry id="guc-collector-min-free-disk" xreflabel="collector_min_free_disk">
    <term><varname>collector_min_free_disk</varname> (<type>integer</type>)
    <indexterm>
     <primary><varname>collector_min_free_disk</varname> configuration parameter</primary>
    </indexterm>
    </term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Sets the free space of the data directory's volume below which the
      collector runs a full collection whenever a database's packs hold more
      than their live bytes. If this value is specified without units, it is
      taken as megabytes. The default, <literal>-1</literal>, is the smaller
      of 10 gigabytes and a tenth of the volume. Doltgrust's
      <literal>min_free_disk</literal>.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>

   <varlistentry id="guc-collector-naptime" xreflabel="collector_naptime">
    <term><varname>collector_naptime</varname> (<type>integer</type>)
    <indexterm>
     <primary><varname>collector_naptime</varname> configuration parameter</primary>
    </indexterm>
    </term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Sets the time the collector waits between its checks of which
      collections are due. If this value is specified without units, it is
      taken as milliseconds. The default is one second
      (<literal>1s</literal>).
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>

   <varlistentry id="guc-collector-target-percent" xreflabel="collector_target_percent">
    <term><varname>collector_target_percent</varname> (<type>integer</type>)
    <indexterm>
     <primary><varname>collector_target_percent</varname> configuration parameter</primary>
    </indexterm>
    </term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Sets how far a database's packs may pass the live bytes its last full
      collection found, as a percentage of them, before the next full
      collection runs, and how far one pack may pass its own live bytes before
      a collection copies its live chunks out and retires it. Doltgrust's
      <literal>target_percent</literal>. The default is 50.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>

   <varlistentry id="guc-collector-young-packs" xreflabel="collector_young_packs">
    <term><varname>collector_young_packs</varname> (<type>integer</type>)
    <indexterm>
     <primary><varname>collector_young_packs</varname> configuration parameter</primary>
    </indexterm>
    </term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Sets how many packs written since a database's last collection make a
      young collection of them due. Doltgrust's
      <literal>YOUNG_PACKS</literal>. The default is 16.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>

   <varlistentry id="guc-collector-young-size" xreflabel="collector_young_size">
    <term><varname>collector_young_size</varname> (<type>integer</type>)
    <indexterm>
     <primary><varname>collector_young_size</varname> configuration parameter</primary>
    </indexterm>
    </term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Sets the size of the packs written since a database's last collection
      that makes a young collection of them due. If this value is specified
      without units, it is taken as kilobytes. Doltgrust's
      <literal>young_size</literal>. The default is 256 megabytes
      (<literal>256MB</literal>).
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>
  </variablelist>
 </sect1>

 <sect1 id="doltgres-config-fold">
  <title>Folding</title>

  <para>
   A fold launcher folds each storage whose unfolded changes pass
   <xref linkend="guc-fold-threshold"/> or grow older than
   <xref linkend="guc-fold-timeout"/>, and each storage a writer needs folded
   to find room in <xref linkend="guc-delta-memory"/>, in fold workers of its
   own, which never count against
   <xref linkend="guc-max-worker-processes"/>.
  </para>

  <variablelist>
   <varlistentry id="guc-fold-threshold" xreflabel="fold_threshold">
    <term><varname>fold_threshold</varname> (<type>integer</type>)
    <indexterm>
     <primary><varname>fold_threshold</varname> configuration parameter</primary>
    </indexterm>
    </term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Sets the size of a storage's unfolded changes at which it is folded.
      If this value is specified without units, it is taken as kilobytes.
      The default of -1 means a sixteenth of
      <xref linkend="guc-delta-memory"/>, read again at each reload.
      Doltgrust's size threshold.
      This parameter can only be set in the
      <filename>postgresql.conf</filename> file or on the server command line.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>

   <varlistentry id="guc-fold-timeout" xreflabel="fold_timeout">
    <term><varname>fold_timeout</varname> (<type>integer</type>)
    <indexterm>
     <primary><varname>fold_timeout</varname> configuration parameter</primary>
    </indexterm>
    </term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Sets the age of a storage's unfolded changes at which it is folded:
      the time since its first change after its last fold, or since that
      fold when the fold left changes a snapshot still needs. It is also the
      longest time the fold launcher waits between its checks. If this value
      is specified without units, it is taken as seconds. Doltgrust's
      <literal>materialize_timeout</literal>. The default is 30 seconds
      (<literal>30s</literal>).
      This parameter can only be set in the
      <filename>postgresql.conf</filename> file or on the server command line.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>

   <varlistentry id="guc-fold-workers" xreflabel="fold_workers">
    <term><varname>fold_workers</varname> (<type>integer</type>)
    <indexterm>
     <primary><varname>fold_workers</varname> configuration parameter</primary>
    </indexterm>
    </term>
    <listitem>
     <para>
      Sets the number of fold worker processes that may run at once, beside
      the fold launcher, in background worker slots the server reserves for
      them. The default is 2.
      This parameter can only be set at server start.
     </para>
    </listitem>
   </varlistentry>
  </variablelist>
 </sect1>

</chapter>
